    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald Stack is delighted to present this charming semi-detached two/three-bedroom cottage, set on a generous 1.01-acre (0.41-hectare) site, offering excellent potential for extension (subject to the necessary planning permission).\n\nIdeally located just 500 metres from the new bypass road and just over 2km from the heritage town of Listowel, the property enjoys the perfect balance of peaceful countryside living with easy access to a wide range of local amenities, including supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, pubs, and both primary and secondary schools.\n\nThe accommodation comprises an inviting lounge/living room, a kitchen/dining room, two ground-floor bedrooms, and a versatile attic bedroom, providing flexible living space to suit a variety of needs.\n\nOutside, the property benefits from a detached block-built shed/garage/workshop, ideal for storage, hobbies, or DIY enthusiasts. The expansive site provides ample outdoor space and presents an excellent opportunity for further development or landscaping.\n\nThe residence is heated by both oil-fired central heating and a solid fuel heating system.\n\nHaving been vacant for approximately two years, the property may qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, subject to the terms, conditions, and eligibility criteria of the scheme.\n\nThis property offers an excellent opportunity for first-time buyers, those seeking a countryside retreat, or purchasers looking for a home with significant potential.\n\nViewing is highly recommended and is strictly by appointment with Sherry FitzGerald Stack"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nKitchen Dining Room - 3.78m x 3.94m\nWith a Stanley oil fired range, linoleum flooring, glazed door leading to the side of the property & window.\n\nLounge/Living Room - 3.98m x 4.56m\nWith open fireplace with tile surround, carpet, shelving, door leading to the front & window.\n\nBathroom - 2.43m x 1.89m\nWith WHB & W/C, bath, linoleum flooring & window.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.21m x 2.39m\nBedroom with carpet & window\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.30m x 2.02m\nBedroom with carpet & window.\n\nBedroom 3 / Attic - 4.50m x 3.34m\nDouble bedroom with wood flooring & a velux window.\n\nExternal Shed - 12m x 4m\nWith masonry walls & steel doors.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Charming 2/3-semi detached cottage set on a generous 1.01-acre (0.41-hectare) site</li><li>Ideal home for first-time buyers, downsizers, or those seeking a property with refurbishment and development potential</li><li>Excellent potential to extend (subject to planning permission)</li><li>Located just 500m from the new bypass road</li><li>Just over 2km from the heritage town of Listowel</li><li>Convenient to supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, pubs, and primary & secondary schools</li><li>Detached block-built garage/workshop providing excellent storage or hobby space</li><li>Oil-fired central heating and solid fuel heating</li><li>Spacious site offering ample outdoor space and future potential</li><li>Vacant for approximately two years and may qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant (subject to eligibility and scheme conditions)</ul>"
      },
